=== F. Symmetry group of the rigid pair (omega, eta), and its action on the splittings ===
d=2: dim Lie algebra preserving omega and eta = 4 (d^2 = 4); all of form diag(a, -a^T): True
d=2: (k, GL(d)-orbit dim, O(d)-orbit dim, k(d-k)) at the splitting span{x_1..x_k, p_k+1..p_d}: [(0, np.int64(0), np.int64(0), 0), (1, np.int64(1), np.int64(1), 1), (2, np.int64(0), np.int64(0), 0)]
d=3: dim Lie algebra preserving omega and eta = 9 (d^2 = 9); all of form diag(a, -a^T): True
d=3: (k, GL(d)-orbit dim, O(d)-orbit dim, k(d-k)) at the splitting span{x_1..x_k, p_k+1..p_d}: [(0, np.int64(0), np.int64(0), 0), (1, np.int64(2), np.int64(2), 2), (2, np.int64(2), np.int64(2), 2), (3, np.int64(0), np.int64(0), 0)]
