K = eta^-1 omega at d = 4: diag = [-1, -1, -1, -1, 1, 1, 1, 1] ; off-diagonal zero: True
  K-eigenspaces (the para-Hermitian polarization): eigenvalue -1 -> x-space, +1 -> p-space; count = 2
  every random V (+) V^perp (d = 4) is K-invariant: True

=== G. Completeness at d = 4 by numerical solve: minimize |A^T B|^2 on orthonormal frames (QR retraction) ===
    (every zero found should be V (+) V^perp: rank A + rank B = d and col A orthogonal to col B)
200 runs: worst residual |A^T B| = 9.9e-15; runs failing (not converged, or rank A + rank B != d): 0; k = rank A distribution: {0: 7, 1: 52, 2: 90, 3: 48, 4: 3}

